    "text": "In the circuit of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> amplifier, a silicon transistor is used. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">V</mtext><mtext>CC</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext><mtext>L</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>k</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> , collector voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then the base resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> should be&nbsp;(Take input voltage drop across Si transistor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> )<br />\r<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/c8496ecb-d2d7-4fde-8dc3-1e8ec607595e.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.92708in;height:1.86042in\" />",
